{"ref":"Job 25","heRef":"איוב כ״ה","isComplex":false,"text":["Bildad the Shuhite said in reply:","<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Dominion and dread are God’s,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Who imposes peace on high.</span>","<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Can the celestial troops be numbered?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">On whom does God’s light not shine?</span>","<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">How can a mortal be in the right before God?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">How can one born of woman be cleared of guilt?</span>","<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Even the moon is not bright,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And the stars are not pure in God’s sight.</span>","<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">How much less a mortal, a worm,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">One born of humans, a maggot.</span>"],"he":["וַ֭יַּעַן בִּלְדַּ֥ד הַשֻּׁחִ֗י וַיֹּאמַֽר׃","הַמְשֵׁ֣ל וָפַ֣חַד עִמּ֑וֹ עֹשֶׂ֥ה שָׁ֝ל֗וֹם בִּמְרוֹמָֽיו׃","הֲיֵ֣שׁ מִ֭סְפָּר לִגְדוּדָ֑יו וְעַל־מִ֝֗י לֹא־יָק֥וּם אוֹרֵֽהוּ׃","וּמַה־יִּצְדַּ֣ק אֱנ֣וֹשׁ עִם־אֵ֑ל וּמַה־יִּ֝זְכֶּ֗ה יְל֣וּד אִשָּֽׁה׃","הֵ֣ן עַד־יָ֭רֵחַ וְלֹ֣א יַאֲהִ֑יל וְ֝כוֹכָבִ֗ים לֹא־זַכּ֥וּ בְעֵינָֽיו׃","אַ֭ף כִּֽי־אֱנ֣וֹשׁ רִמָּ֑ה וּבֶן־אָ֝דָ֗ם תּוֹלֵעָֽה׃&nbsp;<span class=\"mam-spi-pe\">{פ}</span><br>"],"versions":[{"status":"locked","priority":3,"license":"CC-BY-NC","versionNotes":"<a href=\"https://purl.org/jps/rjps-preface\">Preface</a>\n<br><br>\n<a href=\"https://purl.org/jps/gender\">Notes on Gender in Translation</a>\n<br><br>\n<a href=\"https://purl.org/scholar/rjps-comm\">Commentary on Translation Choices in the JPS TANAKH (RJPS)</a>","formatAsPoetry":"","digitizedBySefaria":"","method":"","heversionSource":"","versionUrl":"","versionTitleInHebrew":"","versionNotesInHebrew":"","shortVersionTitle":"Revised JPS, 2023","shortVersionTitleInHebrew":"","extendedNotes":"","extendedNotesHebrew":"","purchaseInformationImage":"https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-physical-edit